  "content": "<h2>I know it's not October yet, but with only a few weeks to go, I thought, <em>why not</em> get into the Halloween spirit a little early? Honestly, I'm that gal who likes spooky things all year round, so only a two-week head start is generous of me. So ready for some bone chilling stories?</h2><figure><p><img src=\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/34093960f4882ac5bec1acc1b963586bb22667f956bd2f2372540eee34136c3e/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w360_h360%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fbuzzfeed_articles_778%2F6a0321cba60a329462182f12ab3720ca.gif\" alt=\"Person with a surprised expression holds their face in their hands, seated indoors\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"360\" height=\"360\" /></p></figure><h2><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@jessokish/video/7650553268120177950\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Over on TikTok</a>, people are sharing the completely unexplainable moments in their lives that made them instantly believe in the paranormal because they were so bizarre that they <em>could only</em> be explained by something supernatural. And honestly, these stories are making my spine tingle. Take a look:</h2><p>Read <em>every</em> story <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@jessokish/video/7650553268120177950\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</p><h2>1.</h2><figure><p><img src=\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/1eb54c2010f485220c4aa9f534e3662de882723f5eb4c7b8cf8816c2a0a89a7f/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w700_h744%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fbuzzfeed_articles_778%2F1215604cc7fb8490fbd58913f9222d54.jpg\" alt=\"A person recalls an eerie experience in Northern California caring for a lady. They describe hearing a soft, distant voice that led to unexplained fear\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"700\" height=\"744\" /></p></figure><h2>2.</h2><figure><p><img src=